{
  "contract": "ito-catalog",
  "version": 3,
  "notes": [
    "Bytes are postcard, the wire of every export result. Entries are MediaEntry values (variant 0 manga, 1 anime, 2 novel).",
    "direction is plugin_to_host, host_to_plugin, or both where a value travels both ways (entries and chapters that pass validation). An entry a plugin receives in get_media_update never carries a catalog.",
    "An entry with repeat_hex is prefix hex, then repeat_hex repeated repeat_count times, then suffix_hex; entries without it are just hex.",
    "expect is the host verdict after decoding; sdk_expect, when present, replaces it for the SDK (decode_error: the SDK cannot decode or build the value).",
    "An entry with canonical_hex is accepted as written; it decodes to the same value as the built case and re-encodes to canonical_hex.",
    "Unknown CatalogScope and CatalogCompleteness discriminants decode to Unknown on both sides. Unknown ContentKind discriminants are rejected (enum.unknown, which only hosts report).",
    "Validation order: catalog.without_chapters, then count.chapters, then each chapter in order (key, title, scanlator name, scanlator id, logical_unit_id, revision, url, lang, volume, chapter, date), then duplicate.key, then scanlator.conflict. The first violation wins.",
    "Strings compare as exact UTF-8 bytes with no normalization; every length is in UTF-8 bytes.",
    "reading_order: lower values are read earlier, values are comparable only within one response, gaps are allowed, equal values mean the same reading position. It is independent of list order, and duplicates are valid.",
    "Numbers are valid when finite and within +-max_abs_number; date_updated (seconds since 1970-01-01 UTC) when finite and within +-max_abs_date.",
    "A present scanlator.id, logical_unit_id and revision is never empty.",
    "codes lists every violation code; enum.unknown is reported by hosts only."
  ],
  "codes": [
    "catalog.without_chapters",
    "count.chapters",
    "length.key",
    "length.title",
    "length.scanlator_name",
    "length.scanlator_id",
    "length.logical_unit_id",
    "length.revision",
    "length.url",
    "length.lang",
    "number.range",
    "number.date",
    "duplicate.key",
    "scanlator.conflict",
    "response.too_large",
    "enum.unknown"
  ],
  "limits": {
    "max_chapters": 20000,
    "max_key_bytes": 512,
    "max_title_bytes": 1024,
    "max_scanlator_name_bytes": 256,
    "max_id_bytes": 256,
    "max_revision_bytes": 256,
    "max_url_bytes": 4096,
    "max_lang_bytes": 35,
    "max_abs_number": 1000000000.0,
    "max_abs_date": 100000000000.0,
    "max_response_bytes": 16777216
  },
